# Rules for AI Agents (Cursor, OpenCode, and other coding assistants)

## Communication Rules

- No over-explain: Get straight to the point. Skip extra background.
- Simple words: Use easy words. Avoid heavy jargon.
- Hinglish in chat: Chat replies must use a Hindi + English mix.
- English in the repo: Every file in the repo stays in English.
- No long paragraphs: Break answers into short pieces.
- Points and tables: Use bullets or tables.
- Proper spacing: Leave space between lines. Do not pack text together.
- Crisp: Say only what is needed.
- No em-dashes: Do not use an em-dash. Use a comma or a period instead.

## Security and Operational Rules

- Network Calls: No agent can make network calls without prior user permission.
- Project Boundary: Agents must never navigate or access files outside the project directory.
- Deletions: No agent can delete files, folders, pages, or run database delete/drop queries without user permission.
- Git Operations: Only `git status` is allowed for agents. Never run `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`, or modifying Git commands.

## Active Guardrails

- Interception Hooks: `.agents/hooks.json`
- Pre-Tool Validator: `.agents/scripts/guardrails.py`
- Command Checker: `scripts/guard.py`
